<section class="at-migration-content">
  <header><small>{{#if isGM}}GAMEMASTER · CAMPAIGN TRANSFER{{else}}MY CHRONICLE{{/if}} · BUILD {{buildVersion}}</small><h1>Import &amp; Export</h1><p>{{#if isGM}}Bring in content, create a backup, or move your campaign.{{else}}Back up or move your own Chronicle.{{/if}}</p></header>
  <nav class="at-migration-tabs" aria-label="Migration workflow"><button type="button" data-action="showImport" class="{{#if isImport}}is-active{{/if}}" aria-pressed="{{isImport}}" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Import</button><button type="button" data-action="showExport" class="{{#if isExport}}is-active{{/if}}" aria-pressed="{{isExport}}" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Export</button></nav>
  {{#if isGM}}
  {{#if error}}<p class="at-migration-error" role="alert">{{error}}</p>{{/if}}
  <section data-migration-panel="import" {{#unless isImport}}hidden{{/unless}}><h2>Import</h2><p>Import into <strong>{{targetWorld}}</strong>. Campaign ZIPs create GM-only copies. Text and Tome packages offer reviewed Create, Update or Skip choices.</p>
    <details {{#unless hasPackage}}open{{/unless}}><summary>Choose a file or paste content</summary>
    <h3>1. Choose your file</h3><input type="file" name="migrationPackage" accept=".zip,.md,.markdown,.txt,.json" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>
    <details><summary>Paste text instead / choose log type</summary><label>Content type<select name="contentMode">{{#each contentModes}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{id}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label><label>Session, Quest log or Tome JSON<textarea name="contentText" rows="8">{{contentText}}</textarea></label></details><p>Campaign ZIP, Tome JSON, Markdown and text are recognized automatically.</p><h3>2. Preview before importing</h3><p>Check what can be imported. Preview does not create documents.</p><button class="at-migration-primary" type="button" data-action="loadPackage" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Preview Import</button>
    </details>{{#if importFileName}}<p>Loaded file: <strong>{{importFileName}}</strong></p>{{/if}}
    {{#if gmPrivateBundle}}<fieldset {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}><legend>Restore GM Notes &amp; Vault</legend><p>Source: {{gmPrivateBundle.source.worldName}}. Merge your private GM notebook and Vault; existing notes remain. Player Chronicles and campaign settings are excluded.</p>{{#unless gmPrivateSameWorld}}<label>Campaign mapping<select name="gmPrivateMapping"><option value="">Choose imported campaign…</option>{{#each gmPrivateMappings}}<option value="{{id}}">{{name}} · {{id}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label><p>For another world, import the campaign ZIP first to reconnect Vault links.</p>{{/unless}}<button type="button" class="at-migration-primary" data-action="restoreGmPrivate">Restore GM Notes &amp; Vault</button>{{#if gmPrivateResult}}<p role="status">Your private GM data is restored.</p>{{/if}}</fieldset>{{/if}}
    {{#if contentPreview}}<fieldset {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}><legend>3. Review content</legend><p>{{contentPreview.modeLabel}} · {{contentPreview.entries.length}} entries · {{contentPreview.resolvedLinks}} resolved links. Existing content can be updated; permissions remain unchanged. New content uses the existing Tome import defaults.</p>
    {{#each contentPreview.entries}}<section class="at-transfer-content-row"><h3>{{name}} · {{kindLabel}}</h3><p>{{#if existingName}}Existing: {{existingName}}{{else}}New entry{{/if}}</p><label>Action<select data-content-choice="{{key}}"><option value="create" {{#if defaultCreate}}selected{{/if}}>Create</option>{{#if canUpdate}}<option value="update" {{#if defaultUpdate}}selected{{/if}}>Update existing</option>{{/if}}<option value="skip">Skip</option></select></label><details><summary>Preview text</summary><pre>{{content}}</pre></details></section>{{/each}}
    {{#if contentPreview.links.length}}<details><summary>Review cross-links</summary>{{#each contentPreview.links}}<label>{{sourceName}} → {{targetName}}<select data-content-link="{{key}}">{{#if resolved}}<option value="apply" {{#if defaultApply}}selected{{/if}}>Apply link</option>{{/if}}<option value="skip" {{#if defaultSkip}}selected{{/if}}>Skip</option></select></label>{{/each}}</details>{{/if}}
    <p data-content-progress role="status">{{#if busy}}Importing content…{{/if}}</p><button type="button" class="at-migration-primary" data-action="applyContent">Do Import</button></fieldset>{{/if}}
    {{#if contentResult}}<p role="status">{{#if contentResult.cancelled}}Content import stopped — saved changes can be undone:{{else}}Content import complete:{{/if}} {{contentResult.created}} created · {{contentResult.updated}} updated · {{contentResult.skipped}} skipped · {{contentResult.failed}} failed · {{contentResult.linksApplied}} links applied.{{#if contentResult.cancelled}} {{contentResult.remaining}} entries remain; preview the retained source again to continue.{{/if}}</p>{{#if contentResult.failures.length}}<details open><summary>Import issues</summary>{{#each contentResult.failures}}<p class="at-migration-error">{{this}}</p>{{/each}}</details>{{/if}}{{/if}}
    <details><summary>Content import history &amp; Undo</summary>{{#if hasContentUndo}}<button type="button" data-action="undoContent" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Undo last content import</button>{{/if}}<button type="button" data-action="clearHistory" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Clear history</button>{{#each importHistory}}<p>{{sourceName}} · {{when}} · {{created}} created · {{updated}} updated {{#if undone}}· Undone{{/if}}</p>{{else}}<p>No content import history yet.</p>{{/each}}<p>Undo applies to the latest text/Tome content import. Campaign ZIP imports create separate copies and retain their source archive.</p></details>
    {{#if hasPackage}}<fieldset {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}><legend>3. Import summary</legend>{{#if skippedDefinitionCount}}<p>{{skippedDefinitionCount}} standard counter/condition definitions are already represented by the target system and will stay in the source package. No duplicate equipment will be created.</p>{{/if}}
      {{#if hasPrivateData}}<details data-account-mapping {{#if accountMappingNeedsReview}}open{{else}}{{#unless hasTafGroups}}open{{/unless}}{{/if}}><summary>Player account mapping ({{userRows.length}} accounts)</summary><p>GM data goes to your current GM account. Multiple old GM accounts may share this importing GM; Player accounts stay separate. Choose an existing account, create a new Player account during import, or keep their documents GM-only. New accounts are reused when retrying. Players move their private Chronicle separately.</p>
      {{#each userRows}}<label>{{name}}{{#if isExportingGM}} · exporting GM{{/if}}<select data-migration-user="{{id}}" {{#if isExportingGM}}disabled{{/if}}><option value="">Choose account…</option><option value="private" {{#if keepPrivate}}selected{{/if}}>Keep GM-only / no account</option>{{#unless isExportingGM}}<option value="new-player" {{#if createPlayer}}selected{{/if}}>Create new Player account</option>{{/unless}}{{#each options}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>{{/each}}</details>
      {{else}}<p>This older ZIP does not contain Campaign Memory or account mapping. Make a new export with qa.3 to include them. Imported documents stay GM-only.</p>{{/if}}
      {{#if hasTafGroups}}<div class="at-migration-notice"><strong>Conversion proposal ready: {{tafCharacters}} Characters · {{tafNpcs}} NPCs.</strong><p>Confirm once with Approve proposal &amp; Import. PC/NPC folders supply proposed types; other unclassified Actors are proposed as NPCs. Existing confirmed source categories are retained. This preview creates no documents or accounts. Import starts only when you approve.</p><p>{{#if tafSceneBase}}Scene tokens will use converted base Actors; their original TAF overrides stay archived.{{else}}Scene token overrides remain for individual review.{{/if}}</p>{{#if newPlayerCount}}<p>{{newPlayerCount}} new Player accounts are proposed. Open Player account mapping to change these proposals before importing.</p>{{/if}}</div><details class="at-taf-batch"><summary>Change proposed groups or Scene handling ({{tafGroups.length}} groups)</summary><p>These are proposals, not confirmed character identities. Change any group that needs a different type; the preview updates automatically.</p>
      <label>Other unclassified Actors<select name="tafFallback"><option value="">Leave for individual review</option><option value="npc" {{#if tafFallbackNpc}}selected{{/if}}>NPC</option><option value="character" {{#if tafFallbackCharacter}}selected{{/if}}>Character</option></select></label>
      {{#each tafGroups}}<label>{{name}} · {{count}} Actors<select data-taf-group="{{id}}"><option value="">Use choice above / review individually</option><option value="character" {{#if isCharacter}}selected{{/if}}>Character</option><option value="npc" {{#if isNpc}}selected{{/if}}>NPC</option></select><small>{{#each sample}}{{this}} · {{/each}}</small></label>{{/each}}
      <p>Compatible core attributes are copied. Remaining values stay readable in Actor Notes; standalone TAF attributes/templates become reference Items with quantity zero. Inventory, portraits and compendium origins are retained. Original rules and Macro triggers stay archived and are never executed.</p>
      <label><input type="checkbox" name="tafSceneBase" {{#if tafSceneBase}}checked{{/if}}> Use converted base Actors for Scene tokens; retain TAF token-specific overrides in the archive only</label></details>{{/if}}
      <p class="at-migration-summary"><strong>{{importReadyCount}} ready · {{importExceptionCount}} need attention.</strong> Ready documents can be imported together. Only unresolved issues need your decision.</p>
      {{#if importPlan.excludedSystemEntries}}<p>{{importPlan.excludedSystemEntries}} system-library entries excluded. The destination system supplies these libraries; they are not active campaign Actors or Items.</p>{{/if}}
      {{#if contactRepairSummary.length}}<fieldset data-contact-repair-summary><legend>Review contact roles before importing</legend><p>These are your selected replacements for missing source links.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Character</th><th>Role</th><th>Selected person</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{#each contactRepairSummary}}<tr data-contact-summary-role="{{role}}"><td>{{actor}}</td><td><strong>{{role}}</strong></td><td>{{person}} {{#if imported}}<small>Imported</small>{{else}}<button type="button" data-action="editContacts" data-contact-source="{{sourceUuid}}">Change</button>{{/if}}{{#if warning}}<p class="at-migration-notice">{{warning}}</p>{{/if}}</td></tr>{{/each}}</tbody></table></fieldset>{{/if}}
      <button class="at-migration-primary" type="button" data-action="importReady" {{#unless canDoImport}}disabled{{/unless}}>{{#if hasTafGroups}}Approve proposal &amp; Import{{else}}Do Import{{/if}}</button>
      <div class="at-import-progress" data-import-progress {{#unless importProgress}}hidden{{/unless}}>
        <p data-import-progress-text role="status" aria-live="polite">{{importProgress.text}}</p>
        <progress aria-label="Import copies saved" max="{{#if importProgress.total}}{{importProgress.total}}{{else}}1{{/if}}" value="{{importProgress.documents}}"></progress>
        {{#if importResult.partial}}<strong>Import stopped — saved copies remain. See the error above.</strong>{{/if}}
      </div>
      <h3>{{#if showAllMappings}}All document details{{else}}Needs your attention{{/if}}</h3>
      {{#each unsupportedGroups}}<p class="at-migration-notice" data-unsupported-group><strong>{{count}} {{type}} · {{sourceType}}</strong>: {{reason}} Original data stays in the package. This is a shared adapter issue, not {{count}} individual decisions.</p>{{/each}}
      {{#each importRows}}<details data-import-row="{{index}}" {{#unless collapseDetails}}open{{/unless}}><summary>{{name}} · {{type}} · {{status}}</summary><p>Source category: {{#if classification.category}}{{classification.category}}{{else}}Not classified — choose per document where required{{/if}} · {{classification.authority}}</p>
        {{#each notes}}<p>{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
        {{#if isTafActor}}<label>taf → Realm Guard Actor type<select name="actorType"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="character" {{#if isCharacter}}selected{{/if}}>Character</option><option value="npc" {{#if isNpc}}selected{{/if}}>NPC</option></select></label>{{/if}}
        {{#each suggestions}}<label>{{label}} ({{key}}): {{value}} / {{max}} · suggested: {{target}}<select data-attribute="{{id}}"><option value="">Keep in archive only</option>{{#each options}}<option value="{{field}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{field}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>{{/each}}
        {{#if contactRepairs.length}}<fieldset data-contact-repairs><legend>Repair missing contact links</legend><p>The original Actor links are missing. Choose the known person for each role, or keep it unresolved. Only Actors in this package are listed; no new NPC is created.</p>{{#each contactRepairs}}<label>{{role}}<select data-contact-repair="{{key}}" data-contact-role="{{role}}" data-contact-owner="{{../sourceUuid}}"><option value="">Keep unresolved</option>{{#each options}}<option value="{{uuid}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{name}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>{{/each}}</fieldset>{{/if}}
        <label><input type="checkbox" name="include" {{#if included}}checked{{/if}} {{#unless canImport}}disabled{{/unless}}> Include this copy</label>
        <label><input type="checkbox" name="approve" {{#if approved}}checked{{/if}}> I reviewed this mapping and its limitations</label>
        {{#if storyPreview}}<details data-story-preview><summary>Readable Biography &amp; mapped sheet fields</summary><dl>{{#each storyPreview.fields}}<dt><strong>{{field}}</strong></dt><dd>{{value}}</dd>{{/each}}</dl>{{#each storyPreview.items}}<p><strong>{{type}}</strong>: {{name}}{{#if rating}} · {{rating}}{{/if}}</p>{{/each}}{{#if storyPreview.contacts.length}}<p>{{storyPreview.contacts.length}} source contacts will be restored under Character → Relationships, reusing imported NPC links where unambiguous.</p>{{/if}}{{#if storyPreview.missingHeaderFields.length}}<p>Not stated unambiguously in the source: {{#each storyPreview.missingHeaderFields}}{{this}} {{/each}}. These header fields remain empty; no age or concept is invented.</p>{{/if}}<p>Full original Biography is retained. Sections without an equivalent field remain readable there; free-text rules are not activated.</p><pre class="at-story-preview">{{storyPreview.text}}</pre></details>{{/if}}
        {{#if data}}<details><summary>Target data preview</summary><pre>{{preview}}</pre><p>All copies begin GM-only. Original source data is additionally archived.</p></details>{{/if}}
      </details>{{else}}<p>No individual decisions needed.</p>{{/each}}
      <details {{#if showAllMappings}}open{{/if}}><summary>Advanced import options</summary>
        <button type="button" data-action="toggleMappings">{{#if showAllMappings}}Show only issues{{else}}Show all document details{{/if}}</button><button type="button" data-action="reviewImport">Update Preview</button><button type="button" data-action="reuseMappings">Apply reviewed field mappings to similar documents</button>
        <details><summary>Choose Character or NPC for unclassified Actors</summary><p>Choose individual exceptions first. Batch choices only apply to Actors without an existing category or target type.</p><button type="button" data-action="unknownNpc">Remaining unclassified Actors are NPCs</button><button type="button" data-action="unknownCharacter">Remaining unclassified Actors are Characters</button></details>
        {{#each importPlan.warnings}}<p>{{this}}</p>{{/each}}
        <p>Private GM data is restored to the importing GM. Old Undo snapshots stay in the private archive; they are not activated in the new world.</p>
    </fieldset>{{/if}}{{#if busy}}<button type="button" data-action="cancel">Stop Import</button>{{/if}}
    {{#if importResult}}<button type="button" data-action="analyzeImported" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Find relationships in imported story</button><p>Uses Tome’s existing text analysis and existing identities. New relationship interpretations go to GM review; this does not create NPCs or confirm claims.</p>{{#if importAnalysis}}<p role="status">{{importAnalysis.sources}} Actor biographies checked · {{importAnalysis.suggestions}} relationship suggestions. Sessions and Quests are queued in Campaign Index. Review suggestions in Campaign Tools → Analysis.</p>{{/if}}<p>{{#if importResult.partial}}Import stopped.{{else}}Import complete.{{/if}} {{importResult.created.length}} copies created · {{importResult.skipped.length}} skipped.{{#if importResult.partial}} {{importResult.remaining}} copies remain. Retry resumes using saved copies.{{/if}}</p>{{#if importResult.portraits.replaced}}<p>{{importResult.portraits.replaced}} missing image references use Realm Guard standard art. Original paths remain in the source archive.</p>{{/if}}{{#each importResult.relationships.progressionNotes}}<p class="at-migration-notice">{{actor}}: {{reason}} Original lifetime totals were retained.</p>{{/each}}<details><summary>Identity map, skipped copies and unresolved references</summary>{{#each importResult.created}}<p>{{sourceUuid}} → {{targetUuid}}</p>{{/each}}{{#each importResult.skipped}}<p>Skipped: {{this}}</p>{{/each}}{{#each importResult.unresolved}}<p>Unresolved: {{this}}</p>{{/each}}</details>{{/if}}
  </section>
  {{#if isImport}}{{#if importResult.alreadyImported.length}}<p>{{importResult.alreadyImported.length}} existing copies or standard folders reused.</p>{{/if}}{{/if}}
  <section data-migration-panel="export" {{#unless isExport}}hidden{{/unless}}><h2>Export</h2><label>What do you want to export?<select name="transferExportKind" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>{{#each exportKinds}}<option value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{label}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>{{#if isCampaignExport}}<p>Create a migration ZIP from <strong>{{targetWorld}}</strong>. Your source world stays intact.</p><h3>1. Choose what to include</h3>
  <div data-migration-selection>
    <fieldset {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}><legend>World content</legend><div class="at-migration-options">{{#each types}}<label><input type="checkbox" name="type" value="{{type}}" {{#if selected}}checked{{/if}}> {{type}} <small>({{count}})</small></label>{{/each}}</div>
      <p>Export preserves Actors and Items unchanged. Map and review them in the destination world.</p>
      <details><summary>Compendium packs — explicitly selected only</summary><div class="at-migration-packs">{{#each packs}}<label><input type="checkbox" name="pack" value="{{id}}" {{#if selected}}checked{{/if}}> {{label}} <small>{{type}} · {{origin}} · {{id}}</small></label>{{else}}<p>No compendium packs available.</p>{{/each}}</div></details>
      {{#if excludedPacks.length}}<details><summary>{{excludedPacks.length}} system libraries automatically excluded</summary><p>System libraries and Quick NPC starter templates are supplied by the game system. Campaign Actors and your own compendiums remain exportable.</p>{{#each excludedPacks}}<p>{{label}}</p>{{/each}}</details>{{/if}}
      <details><summary>Advanced export options</summary><label>Destination system (optional)<input name="targetSystem" value="{{targetSystem}}" placeholder="For planning only"></label></details>
      <label>Images and audio<select name="mediaMode"><option value="references" {{#unless includeMedia}}selected{{/unless}}>References only — files must be moved separately</option><option value="include" {{#if includeMedia}}selected{{/if}}>Include accessible media files in ZIP</option></select></label>
      <p>Included media is limited to 64 MiB per file and 512 MiB total. Unavailable files remain references and appear in the export report.</p>
    </fieldset>
  </div>
  <h3>2. Preview before downloading</h3><button class="at-migration-primary" type="button" data-action="analyze" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Preview Export</button>
  <p data-migration-progress role="status" aria-live="polite">{{#if busy}}Working in the background…{{else}}{{#if error}}Operation stopped — see the error above.{{else}}Ready{{/if}}{{/if}}</p>
  {{#if hasAnalysis}}
    <section><h2>Export preview</h2><p><strong>{{manifest.source.worldName}}</strong> · {{manifest.source.systemId}} {{manifest.source.systemVersion}} · Foundry {{manifest.source.foundryVersion}}</p>
    <p><strong>{{manifest.totalDocuments}} documents selected.</strong> Actor and Item data is preserved in the ZIP; target compatibility is checked when importing.</p>
    <h3>3. Download your ZIP</h3><button class="at-migration-primary" type="button" data-action="download" {{#unless canDownload}}disabled{{/unless}}>Download Export ZIP</button>
    <details><summary>Technical export details</summary>
    <div class="at-migration-counts"><span>{{ready}} Ready</span><span>{{needsReview}} Needs review</span><span>{{unmapped}} Unmapped</span><span>{{unsupported}} Unsupported</span><span>{{unresolved}} Unresolved references</span><span>{{assets}} Media references</span></div>
    <p>{{manifest.totalDocuments}} documents · {{manifest.totalIdentities}} identities · {{excluded}} Chronicle documents excluded</p>
    <p class="at-migration-notice"><strong>Private GM package.</strong> Document ownership IDs and all selected document data are preserved. This ZIP is not player-safe. Destination user mapping must be reviewed before restoring visibility.</p>
    <details><summary>Documents and conversion status</summary><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Source</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{#each documents}}<tr><td>{{name}} {{#if review}}<small>{{review}}</small>{{/if}}</td><td>{{type}}</td><td>{{pack}}</td><td>{{status}}</td></tr>{{/each}}</tbody></table></details>
    <details><summary>References outside this selection ({{unresolved}})</summary><ul>{{#each unresolvedRows}}<li><code>{{sourceUuid}}</code> → <code>{{targetUuid}}</code> <small>{{path}}</small></li>{{else}}<li>All recognized references are included.</li>{{/each}}</ul></details>
    <details><summary>System / module dependencies</summary><ul>{{#each dependencies}}<li>{{this}}</li>{{else}}<li>No dependencies detected.</li>{{/each}}</ul></details>
    <details><summary>Image and audio references ({{assets}})</summary><ul>{{#each mediaRows}}<li><code>{{source}}</code></li>{{else}}<li>No media references detected.</li>{{/each}}</ul></details>
    </details>
    </section>
  {{/if}}
  {{#if exported}}<section><h2>Export complete</h2><p>The ZIP contains manifest.json, campaign.json and any included media. Original paths are retained and mapped to package files. SHA-256 checksums identify the exported payload and media.</p>{{#each mediaIssues}}<p class="at-migration-error">{{source}}: {{error}} — preserved as a reference.</p>{{else}}<p>No media read failures reported.</p>{{/each}}</section>{{/if}}
  {{#if busy}}<button type="button" data-action="cancel">Stop Export</button>{{/if}}
  {{else}}{{#if isGmPrivateExport}}<p>Back up your private GM notebook, scratchpad, contextual notes, Vault and reveal queue. Player Chronicles and campaign settings are excluded. Restore this JSON through the Import tab.</p>{{else}}{{#if isPlayerSafeExport}}<p class="at-migration-notice">Player-safe export uses discovered, non-GM-only content with Observer-or-higher default Foundry ownership. User-specific permissions can be stricter. Review the file before sharing outside your group.</p>{{/if}}<p>Tome content packages can be imported back into Tome. Player-safe content uses the existing visibility filters. Private GM archives remain backup/reference files; use a campaign ZIP for restoration into another world.</p>{{/if}}<button type="button" class="at-migration-primary" data-action="analyze" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Preview Export</button>{{#if jsonExport}}<p>{{jsonExport.bytes}} bytes ready · {{jsonExport.kind}}</p><button type="button" class="at-migration-primary" data-action="downloadContent" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Download Export JSON</button><button type="button" data-action="copyContent" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Copy JSON</button>{{/if}}{{/if}}
  </section>
  {{else}}
  {{#if personalError}}<p class="at-migration-error" role="alert">{{personalError}}</p>{{/if}}
  {{#if isImport}}<section data-personal-transfer><h2>Import my Chronicle</h2><p>Choose your own Chronicle file from the old world. Your GM maps your old account once; no simultaneous login is needed. Existing notes remain, encrypted notes keep the same passphrase, and shared versions are not sent again.</p><label>Chronicle JSON<input name="chronicleFile" type="file" accept=".json" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}></label><label>Campaign move<select name="chronicleReceipt" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>{{#each receipts}}<option value="{{packageId}}">{{sourceWorldName}} · {{sourceWorldId}}</option>{{/each}}</select></label>{{#unless receipts.length}}<p>For a campaign move, your GM needs to map your old account. A backup from this same account and world can be restored directly.</p>{{/unless}}<button type="button" class="at-migration-primary" data-action="personalImport" {{#if busy}}disabled{{/if}}>Import my Chronicle</button>{{#if personalResult}}<p role="status">{{#if personalResult.alreadyImported}}This file is already imported.{{else}}Your Chronicle is imported. No shared versions were sent.{{/if}}</p>{{/if}}</section>
  {{else}}<section data-personal-transfer><h2>Export my Chronicle</h2><p>Save your own notes and bookmarks for backup or a campaign move. Encrypted notes stay encrypted. Keep this file yourself.</p><button type="button" class="at-migration-primary" data-action="personalExport">Download my Chronicle</button></section>{{/if}}
  {{/if}}
</section>
